*.log

# Generated artifacts (CQ-6). The whitepaper's source of truth is
# docs/WHITEPAPER-v2.1.md plus SigilKit_Whitepaper.txt — both plain text, both diffable.
# The PDF is a derived export and was a 1.5 MB binary in history with no diff value;
# keep it on disk locally, regenerate it for a release, attach it to the release.
SigilKit_Whitepaper.pdf
fleet-manifest.json

# Local audit stores. The indexer's default output is ./sigilkit-audit.db, so a stray
# `sigilkit-indexer backfill` would otherwise show up as an untracked binary.
*.db
*.db-shm
*.db-wal

# Agent scratch: probes, sandboxes, one-shot debug scripts and backup copies. During the
# 2026-09 audit round 301 files under .sc-gate-sandbox/ and .codebuddy/ were untracked
# AND unignored (73% of all untracked paths), so a single `git add -A` would have committed
# 301 agent session/sandbox files into the repo. Patterns are deliberately broad because
# these are throwaway by construction; nothing the project ships matches them
# (verified: `git ls-files | grep -E 'probe|\.bak-|^tmp-|\.tmp|\.mcp-|^scratch-'` is empty).
# `.codebuddy/` is listed explicitly rather than via a glob because it was previously only
# PARTIALLY ignored (`.codebuddy/models.json` alone, line 19) — the rest of the directory
# (49 team/session files) was never covered.
.codebuddy/
.sc-gate-sandbox/
.sigilkit-junction-probe/
# Agent working artifacts from the 2026-09/10 review waves: audit manifests, slices,
# work orders, and per-agent result reports. Scratch by construction, not deliverables.
/.audit-*
/.ck-*
/.docgate-*
/.perf-audit/
*_probe*
.*probe*
probe-*
_probe*
_probe?.???
*.crperf*
.bak-*
tmp-*
*.tmp
*.tmp.*
.mcp-*
.vitest-perf.json
.vitest-recheck.json
scratch-*
# scripts/ scratch: the audit round created 15 `_`-prefixed throwaway scripts (_probe1..7,
# _calibrate, _census, _count-forge, _forge-shim.ps1, _forge-stub, _inject, _sandbox-setup,
# _triage). `*_probe*` does NOT match these: it requires `<chars>_probe<chars>`, and a name
# that STARTS with `_probe` has no leading characters for `*` to consume. Caught by sc-clean
# via `git check-ignore --no-index scripts/_probe1.mjs` returning "not ignored" — the rule
# looked correct in the file but matched nothing in practice. `scripts/lib/` is the only
# non-underscore new dir and is unaffected. Verified: `git ls-files scripts/ | grep /_` is
# empty, so no tracked script is at risk.
scripts/_*.mjs
scripts/_*.ps1
scripts/._*
scripts/.bench-probe-*

# Repo-root scratch, same family as the scripts/ rules above but pinned to the root with a
# leading `/` so a nested `PROJECT-MAP.md` or `_notes.txt` in a real source directory is not
# accidentally ignored. The 2026-09 audit left twelve root files untracked AND unignored; all
# twelve are regenerable (a vitest log, a one-off PowerShell counter, and two dated audit
# snapshots), so none of them belong in history.
/.tmp-*
/_*.txt
/PROJECT-MAP.md
/FILE-MANIFEST.md

# Docker compose local state
data/
